<title>USA: Quick &amp; Reilly hires bank to seek sale-WSJ.</title>
<headline>Quick &amp; Reilly hires bank to seek sale-WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brokerage firm Quick &amp; Reilly Group Inc has hired an investment banker to solicit a buyer for the company, the Wall Street Journal reported, citing people familiar with the situation.</p>
<p>The paper said in its electronic edition that the brokerage could fetch as much as $1.5 billion in a sale.</p>
<p>Quick &amp; Reilly's stock rose 2-11/16 Monday to close at 29-5/16.</p>
<p>Quick &amp; Reilly officials were not immediately available to comment.</p>
</text>
